{"id":"thebez","name":"Thebez","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:thebez"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Thebez","text":"Brightness, a place some 11 miles north-east of Shechem, on the road to Scythopolis, the modern Tabas. Abimelech led his army against this place, because of its participation in the conspiracy of the men of Shechem; but as he drew near to the strong tower to which its inhabitants had fled for safety, and was about to set fire to it, a woman cast a fragment of millstone at him, and “all to brake his skull” i.e., “altogether brake,” etc. His armourbearer thereupon “thrust him through, and he died” (Judg. 9:50-55)."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H40","lemma":"אֲבִימֶלֶךְ","xlit":"ʼĂbîymelek","gloss":"Abimelek, the name of two Philistine kings and of two Is","kjv":"Abimelech","count":6,"share":0.75},{"strong":"H8405","lemma":"תֵּבֵץ","xlit":"Têbêts","gloss":"Tebets, a place in Palestine","kjv":"Thebez","count":2,"share":0.25},{"strong":"H6400","lemma":"פֶּלַח","xlit":"pelach","gloss":"a slice","kjv":"piece","count":2,"share":0.25},{"strong":"H4026","lemma":"מִגְדָּל","xlit":"migdâl","gloss":"a tower","kjv":"castle, flower, tower","count":2,"share":0.25},{"strong":"H7393","lemma":"רֶכֶב","xlit":"rekeb","gloss":"a vehicle","kjv":"chariot, millstone, multitude, wagon","count":2,"share":0.25},{"strong":"H5066","lemma":"נָגַשׁ","xlit":"nâgash","gloss":"to be or come near","kjv":"approach, bring, come, give place","count":2,"share":0.25}],"verses":["Judg.9.50","Judg.9.52","Judg.9.53","Judg.9.55","Judg.9.56","2Sam.11.21","Judg.9.51","Judg.9.54"],"related":[{"id":"abimelech","type":"lexical","strong":"H40","why":"both lead with אֲבִימֶלֶךְ (H40)"},{"id":"conspiracy","type":"lexical","strong":"H40","why":"both lead with אֲבִימֶלֶךְ (H40)"},{"id":"cowardice","type":"lexical","strong":"H40","why":"both lead with אֲבִימֶלֶךְ (H40)"},{"id":"gaal","type":"lexical","strong":"H40","why":"both lead with אֲבִימֶלֶךְ (H40)"},{"id":"ju